---
import ContentLayout from '@/layouts/content-layout.astro'
import {
	ENGAGEMENT_TERMS,
	FULL_TIME_ENGINEER_SALARY,
	HOURLY_RATE,
	MVP_BUILD_FROM,
	RESCUE_AUDIT,
	RETAINER_TIERS,
	STRATEGY_SESSION,
	WEEKLY_CAPACITY_HOURS,
	formatUsd,
} from '@/lib/pricing'

const cheapest = RETAINER_TIERS[0]
const priciest = RETAINER_TIERS[RETAINER_TIERS.length - 1]
const techLead = RETAINER_TIERS.find((t) => t.id === 'tech-lead')!
const monthlySalary = Math.round(FULL_TIME_ENGINEER_SALARY / 12)
const salaryShare = Math.round((techLead.monthlyPrice / monthlySalary) * 100)

const description = `One rate for everything: ${formatUsd(HOURLY_RATE)} an hour. Monthly plans from ${formatUsd(cheapest.monthlyPrice)}, MVP builds from ${formatUsd(MVP_BUILD_FROM)}, and a ${formatUsd(RESCUE_AUDIT.price)} audit for AI-built apps. See how it compares to a ${formatUsd(FULL_TIME_ENGINEER_SALARY / 1000)}k full-time engineer.`
---

<ContentLayout title="Pricing and Rates (2026) | Ilzam, AI-Native Software Engineer" description={description}>
	<div class="flex items-center gap-3">
		<span class="rounded-sm bg-muted px-2 py-0.5 text-xs font-medium uppercase">Pricing</span>
		<span class="text-xs text-muted-foreground">Updated October 2026</span>
	</div>

	<h1 class="mt-4 text-3xl font-light leading-tight tracking-tight md:text-4xl">
		Pricing and Rates
	</h1>

	<p class="mt-6 text-lg leading-relaxed">
		Everything I do is billed at one rate, {formatUsd(HOURLY_RATE)} an hour. Monthly plans run from
		{formatUsd(cheapest.monthlyPrice)} to {formatUsd(priciest.monthlyPrice)} depending on how many
		hours you need. A first version of your product (an MVP) starts at {formatUsd(MVP_BUILD_FROM)},
		and if you only need one decision made well, a single {STRATEGY_SESSION.minutes}-minute strategy
		session is {formatUsd(STRATEGY_SESSION.price)}.
	</p>
	<p class="mt-4 leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground">{ENGAGEMENT_TERMS}</p>
	<p class="mt-4 leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground">
		Every plan gets the same way of working. AI agents handle most of the typing, I make the
		decisions and review every change before it ships, and you own all of the code.
	</p>

	<!-- Monthly plans -->
	<section class="mt-10">
		<h2 class="text-xl font-semibold">Monthly plans</h2>
		<div class="mt-6 grid gap-4 md:grid-cols-3">
			{
				RETAINER_TIERS.map((tier) => (
					<div class="flex flex-col rounded-lg border p-5">
						<p class="font-medium">{tier.name}</p>
						<p class="mt-3 text-3xl font-light tracking-tight">
							{formatUsd(tier.monthlyPrice)}
							<span class="text-sm text-muted-foreground"> / month</span>
						</p>
						<p class="mt-1 text-xs text-muted-foreground">
							About {tier.hoursPerMonth} hours, roughly {Math.round(tier.hoursPerMonth / 4)} a week
						</p>
						<p class="mt-4 text-sm leading-relaxed">{tier.summary}</p>
						<ul class="mt-4 flex-1 space-y-2 text-sm text-muted-foreground">
							{tier.includes.map((item) => (
								<li class="flex gap-2">
									<span class="mt-2 size-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-foreground" />
									{item}
								</li>
							))}
						</ul>
						<p class="mt-4 text-xs italic text-muted-foreground">Best for: {tier.bestFor}</p>
					</div>
				))
			}
		</div>

		<div class="mt-4 rounded-lg bg-muted/50 p-5">
			<p class="font-medium">
				Not ready for a monthly plan? {STRATEGY_SESSION.name}, {formatUsd(STRATEGY_SESSION.price)} one-off
			</p>
			<ul class="mt-3 space-y-1 text-sm text-muted-foreground">
				{STRATEGY_SESSION.includes.map((item) => <li>{item}</li>)}
			</ul>
		</div>
	</section>

	<!-- Hourly rate -->
	<section class="mt-12">
		<h2 class="text-xl font-semibold">Hourly rate</h2>
		<p class="mt-4 leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground">
			{formatUsd(HOURLY_RATE)} an hour, on every plan and every build. You choose how much of my time
			you need, and I bill by the month so you can message me when something comes up without
			watching a meter.
		</p>
		<div class="mt-6 overflow-x-auto">
			<table class="w-full text-left text-sm">
				<thead>
					<tr class="border-b">
						<th class="py-3 pr-4 font-medium">Plan</th>
						<th class="py-3 pr-4 font-medium">Per month</th>
						<th class="py-3 pr-4 font-medium">Hours a month</th>
						<th class="py-3 font-medium">About per week</th>
					</tr>
				</thead>
				<tbody class="text-muted-foreground">
					{
						RETAINER_TIERS.map((tier) => (
							<tr class="border-b">
								<td class="py-3 pr-4 text-foreground">{tier.name}</td>
								<td class="py-3 pr-4">{formatUsd(tier.monthlyPrice)}</td>
								<td class="py-3 pr-4">~{tier.hoursPerMonth}</td>
								<td class="py-3">~{Math.round(tier.hoursPerMonth / 4)} hours</td>
							</tr>
						))
					}
				</tbody>
			</table>
		</div>
		<p class="mt-4 leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground">
			I keep about {WEEKLY_CAPACITY_HOURS} hours a week for client work, so the {priciest.name} plan
			goes to one client at a time. If it is taken, the smaller plans usually still have room.
		</p>
	</section>

	<!-- Savings -->
	<section class="mt-12">
		<h2 class="text-xl font-semibold">Is a monthly plan cheaper than hiring?</h2>
		<p class="mt-4 leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground">
			A full-time senior engineer in the US is a {formatUsd(FULL_TIME_ENGINEER_SALARY)}+ salary
			commitment. That is about {formatUsd(monthlySalary)} a month before equity, benefits, and
			recruiting. The {techLead.name} plan is {formatUsd(techLead.monthlyPrice)} a month, roughly
			{salaryShare}% of the salary alone, and you can stop it with 2 weeks' notice instead of
			running a hiring and firing process.
		</p>
		<p class="mt-4 leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground">
			It stops being the right fit when you need someone full time for months on end. The
			{priciest.name} plan tops out at about {WEEKLY_CAPACITY_HOURS} hours a week, and past that a
			full-time hire who owns the role long term is often the better investment. I'll tell you when
			you've reached that point, and I can help you hire that person.
		</p>
	</section>

	<!-- Cost drivers -->
	<section class="mt-12">
		<h2 class="text-xl font-semibold">What changes the cost</h2>
		<div class="mt-6 space-y-4">
			<div class="rounded-lg bg-muted/50 p-5">
				<p class="font-medium">How much of my time you need</p>
				<p class="mt-1 text-sm leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground">
					This matters most, which is why the plans are sized by hours. A bigger plan means
					I'm more involved in planning the work, checking it, and hiring.
				</p>
			</div>
			<div class="rounded-lg bg-muted/50 p-5">
				<p class="font-medium">Whether I'm advising or building</p>
				<p class="mt-1 text-sm leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground">
					The {cheapest.name} plan covers advice, code review, and small fixes. {techLead.name} adds
					leading your developers and building features when they need more hands. If you want me
					building every week, that's the {priciest.name} plan, or a one-time build of your first
					version (an MVP) starting from {formatUsd(MVP_BUILD_FROM)}. To see what your product would cost to build, try the
					<a href="/tool/mvp-cost-estimator/" class="underline underline-offset-4 hover:text-foreground">app and software development cost calculator</a>.
				</p>
			</div>
			<div class="rounded-lg bg-muted/50 p-5">
				<p class="font-medium">Whether you already have something built</p>
				<p class="mt-1 text-sm leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground">
					If you built a prototype with Lovable, Bolt, Cursor, or an earlier developer and it is
					starting to break, start with a {formatUsd(RESCUE_AUDIT.price)} {RESCUE_AUDIT.name}. Within
					{RESCUE_AUDIT.businessDays} business days you get a plain-English report and one fixed price
					for the fixes, with the audit fee taken off. You know the full cost before any work starts.
				</p>
			</div>
		</div>
	</section>

	<!-- CTA -->
	<section class="mt-12 rounded-lg border p-6">
		<h2 class="text-xl font-semibold">Not sure which plan fits?</h2>
		<p class="mt-2 leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground">
			Book a free 30-minute intro call. No pitch, no pressure, just a real conversation about what
			you're building.
		</p>
		<a
			href="https://cal.com/ilzam/intro"
			target="_blank"
			rel="noopener noreferrer"
			class="mt-4 inline-flex rounded-full bg-foreground px-5 py-2 text-sm font-medium text-background transition-opacity hover:opacity-90"
		>
			Book a free intro call
		</a>
	</section>
</ContentLayout>
